  /// security responses to potentially unwanted traffic to your user pool,
  /// set to ENFORCED . For more information, see Adding advanced security to
  /// a user pool . To activate this setting, your user pool must be on the
  /// Plus tier .
  pub user_pool_add_ons: UserPoolAddOnsType? = None
  /// Case sensitivity of the username input for the selected sign-in option.
  /// When case sensitivity is set to False (case insensitive), users can sign
  /// in with any combination of capital and lowercase letters. For example,
  /// username , USERNAME , or UserName , or for email, email@example.com or
  /// EMaiL@eXamplE.Com . For most use cases, set case sensitivity to False
  /// (case insensitive) as a best practice. When usernames and email
  /// addresses are case insensitive, Amazon Cognito treats any variation in
  /// case as the same user, and prevents a case variation from being assigned
